king as an office  environment and really what it comes  down to is this chair is extremely  comfortable and it's extremely versatile  it works just as well in office as it  does in my living room though it does  take up a good amount of space um we  specifically went for the xl because of  the size of my frame 6'4 240 and the  chair basically holds up really really  well my wife's been using it as well  she's obviously significantly smaller  than that and she even commented about  how the chair feels big so you can  definitely tell that this chair is made  for the size of you know a taller person  the first thing that really kind of  struck me opening it up is it's heavy  you know the build quality is  outstanding you can tell from  everything from the brush metal of the  base blades through the you know we  talked about the stitching and you've  got a better look at the foam padding in  the earlier parts of the video  and every part of it feels luxury  my written review i called it the  ferrari of gaming chairs and that's  really the case here and it even comes  with my own set of driving gloves  so they definitely have a lot of kind of  small stylistic touches that are really  they feel unnecessary uh but they feel  welcome addition so these gloves are you  know at this point they're pretty dirty  with grease the  whole of the central axis as well grease  as are the wheels and so what we found  basically was there's a reason for them  being in here and it's to keep yourself  clean when you're working it  my son and i  built the chair together he's two years  old and he is in love with it so if you  have kids there's a great chair you use  that with  what i really just kind of wanted to  highlight is that this is an expensive  chair it is almost 500  and  it feels like it it  feels like money well spent i've had  racing chairs before and  in fact i broke a gaming chair uh within  about six months of use the plastic of  the base plate cracked and i can't  imagine that happening with this chair  it's  feels together it feels very  strong structurally  and there's no sense of loss of balance  when i go into the floor recline mode  versus using it in an upright position  the  armrests i mentioned have a very  satisfying quick sound so you can hear  it here  and i ended up fidgeting with them way  too often  the real only downside to the chair that  i found besides it being expensive of  course is the neck support so you can  see that i'm sitting in an upright  position and it rests right between my  shoulder blades so i can  pull it up and use it like this  but it immediately locks back down if i  lean forward so i would have liked a  little bit more customization in terms  of being able to set the position of the  neck support  but it's extremely comfortable in the  horizontal position it feels like i'm  reclining on a pillow it's  firm but soft so pretty much everything  i'd want in a pillow so  uh it works out really nicely in the  horizontal mode and  it works fine in an office environment  just a little annoying that it  constantly slides back down  what it really comes down to with this  chair is  is it worth the price and  from my experience over the last 10 days  i have to say yes i can't imagine  meeting another chair at any point in  time again  uh as long as i have this one because  nothing  no part of it feels like there is a  structural breaking point or a  structural weak point that could  collapse at any point i mentioned before  that i have a two-year-old so i picked  the white one uh specifically so i can  look and see you know  how easy is it for him to get jam hands  all over it  and the answer is not particularly  albeit he hasn't  poured an entire box of juice on top of  it but so far there's been no sign of  any stain or residue from his  interactions with the chairs so that was  something i was concerned about but it's  held up very very well so if you're in  the market if you are a larger  person you know